At the accepted coexistence point the uniform and localized minima are nondegenerate, the localized-minus-uniform energy crossing is transverse, and the other configurations are separated from the finite minimizing set by a positive compact-complement gap. The implicit-function theorem plus continuity therefore gives an **open D12-symmetric spectral neighborhood** in which the two stable branches and a nearby transverse first-order coexistence event persist. The theorem is qualitative: no explicit maximal radius is claimed.

